WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.020
The Beverly Hillbillies.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:41.620
Hi, Miss Jane. You know, I never had a chance to thank you proper for taking Ellie Mae under your wing.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:47.280
Oh, my pleasure. She's a wonderful roommate, and the girls at the bank are just delighted to have her working with them.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.700
Oh, am I pleased to hear that. Come on in.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.960
Oh, no, thank you. I just dropped by to deliver some of Ellie's friends.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.080
Where is it?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.400
They're in the car. You see, there's a rule in my apartment building against keeping pets.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.710
No, some she acquired after she got there.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.390
Dad's only made for you.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.480
She sees one stray critter that's got a home right now.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:29.350
Is that all of them?

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:29.890
No.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.420
There's a surprise package.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.120
This box.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.980
Well, I'll be doggone.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.780
I believe that doesn't.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:38.580
Oh, hold on.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:39.390
One more.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.380
One more what?

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:41.780
I don't know.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:42.920
It ain't hatched out yet.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:46.540
It is either a goose or a duck.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:47.800
I just hope it ain't an alligator.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.930
I didn't realize you were filling in for Miss Hathaway.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:10.670
Oh, yes, sir. She went to take some things up to my pal.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.690
And how is your sainted father? Well, I hope?

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.940
Oh, yes, sir. Just fine and dandy.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.220
Oh, my. Well, your typing is coming along just beautifully.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.240
Just look at that. Dear sir.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.700
Just one thing, I notice you're only using the small letters.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.540
I meant the use of capitals.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.220
Are you familiar with the capitals?

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.740
Oh, yes, sir, some of them.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.320
The capital of Arkansas is Little Rock.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.200
And the capital of...

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.720
Oh, yes, sir, it is.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.760
And the capital of Missouri is Jefferson City.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.120
But there's another capital.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:50.630
Let me show you what I mean.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.700
Now, you push that, and you press that,

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.170
and you get big D.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.520
Oh, yes, sir, big D.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.780
That stands for Dallas.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.400
What I'm showing you is the capital.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.260
Oh, no, sir.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.480
The capital of Texas is Austin.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:08.640
Wonderful.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.250
How soon will Miss Hathaway be back?

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:12.610
Any minute now.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.370
So I'd better hurry and get none of these letters.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.560
Well, who's learning to type?

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.350
And doing just beautiful.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:29.530
Oh, my.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.380
You're not conserving paper.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:34.530
You know, Chief, this is a potential fire hazard.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.610
You've just given me a wonderful idea,

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:40.750
and I'll just stand right over here and see if I can find a match.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.830
Really? Relax.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.950
I'll get these letters out for you in no time.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.430
Don't ever leave your post again.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.750
Well, I had an errand to do.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:51.350
Next time, that only may do it.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:52.230
Can't drive.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.550
She can't type, either.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:55.670
Give her time.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:57.430
Someday she'll be a great help to you.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.960
Yes, if I ever need to know the capital...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:07.460
of Arkansas. What? Oh, never mind. Get those letters out. This girl is not as much use for me as the

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:13.960
Supreme Sacriliac. She can't type, she can't do shorthand, she can't do filings, run a computer,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:20.280
she can't count money. She's a totally useless female. Who's that, Mr. Graydale? What? Who?

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:27.280
Oh, my wife. Good to see you, Mr. Crampitz. To what do I owe the honor of your visit? Well,

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.960
Well, I don't highly reckon you'd call it an honor, I just come to...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:42.350
deposit some money well that's an honor and the pleasure who did say a deposit yeah somebody sent

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:47.580
me a check a while back and i clean forgot about it well put it right there royalties from your

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:54.520
oil wells no doubt it could be i recollect it was drawn on a bank in tulsa new york texas one

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:59.690
them big places. How much money? I don't remember. It was, uh, what?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.760
Ten, twelve million?

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:01.560
Ten, twelve million?

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:02.780
Yeah, somewhere in that neighborhood.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.140
I haven't misplaced that thing again.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.040
Well, here, here, let me help you, look.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.680
It ain't in my pants pocket.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:14.460
Look, look, look, look, look.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.620
There's a hole in your shirt pocket.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:17.740
Maybe it went in here.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:18.820
All right?

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.320
Mr. Dryer, did he?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.520
I'd appreciate if you didn't undress me,

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:26.760
somebody's allowed to walk in.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:28.980
Who is it?

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:32.510
Come in, come in.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:37.020
You, Mr. Drysdale.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.580
Oh, Jed, check that come to you a while back.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.520
Yeah, I was looking for that thing.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:44.280
I must have lost it.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.030
That's exactly what you done.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:49.320
While you were sitting on the grinder wheel, pumping away,

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:50.860
it fell out of your pocket.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:51.860
You found it.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.340
Ellie's ape found it.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:54.440
Good, good.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.820
But he scampered up the tree with it,

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:58.200
and I couldn't catch him.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.160
Too bad Ellie wasn't there.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:02.910
That girl climbed like a squirrel.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:04.730
What happened to the check?

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:08.530
Well, I sent Jethro up the tree to take it away from the ape.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:09.370
Good, good.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.160
But coming down, he dropped the check,

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.750
and Ellie's raccoon grabbed it and run under the house with it.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:20.460
Granny, one of these days, I got to plug up that hole.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.430
Is the check still under the house?

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:24.160
No.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.530
Ellie's bobcat was under there.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.630
And he chased the raccoon out, so I grabbed it.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.800
You grabbed the check?

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:32.900
No, the bobcat.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.180
I didn't want him to catch the raccoon.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:39.000
Please, please, where is the check?

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.980
Right here in my reticule.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:42.700
Would you like to have it?

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.600
Would Reagan want to be governor again?

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.720
That's an interesting question.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.180
What do you think, Jed?

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:50.940
You got me.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.070
Let's ask Miss Jane what she thinks.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:54.540
Good, I think.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.840
I'm sure I still have my first textbook on typing.

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.570
Oh, maybe it's over here.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.600
I sure do hate to put you to all this trouble, Miss Jane.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:10.920
It's no trouble at all, Allie.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:12.250
Here it is.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:18.000
Can I take you back to the bank with me in practice?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.360
Oh, that's the whole idea.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:22.520
Oh, and speaking of the bank, our lunch hour is almost over.

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:29.970
Finney, you will be happy to know that we are not cooking...

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.930
lunch in the apartment what i'll be happy you know is you get rid of the zoo it's all

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:39.530
taken care of i assure you girl collects animals the way you collect books speaking of books mr

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:44.550
finney i wonder if you could possibly repair the lock on this cabinet i have some rather rare

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:49.550
additions on ornithology what's that miss jenny it's a study of birds don't tell her she'll bring

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:54.990
some home well come on ellie we better go and don't bring along any critters as you call them

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:58.800
Yes, sir, Mr. Finney. I'm sure I'm sorry you don't like animals.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.540
It's all right. I don't like people either.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:16.130
I'll talk to you alone.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:17.170
Are you?

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:18.630
You talking to me, Mr. Finney?

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:20.070
You know good and well I am.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.420
Now come in here.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:23.970
It's a little matter of rent I want to discuss.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:25.000
Thank you.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:29.160
Well, I'm lucky.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:29.920
Sorry.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:30.840
I didn't realize you were.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.760
Speaking of me, you see, I've, uh...

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:34.150
Change my name.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.760
What, again? What do you call yourself this week?

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:37.670
Paul.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:38.450
Redford.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:39.920
Thank you.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.500
Last week you were Robert Newman.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:45.100
Yeah, well, Paul Newman and Robert Redford have done pretty well with those names, so I...

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:46.450
I figured it might work for me.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.070
Why don't you call yourself Frank Sinatra?

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:49.590
I did.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:50.900
except for one week.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:51.840
Do you get any work?

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:53.230
For one week.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:54.840
Frank got a little uptight.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.060
You see, I...

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:57.540
Sing as well as act.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:58.000
Oh.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.120
Oh, great.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:08:59.940
See you right.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:01.250
Employed in two fields, huh?

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:01.630
Three.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:03.210
I also dance.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:05.230
As a matter of fact, last month for a couple of weeks,

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.850
I was Fred Kelly and Jean Astaire.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.290
Look, under any name,

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.670
he owe me three months back rent.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:11.720
Really?

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:13.420
Oh, well, well.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:14.700
I'll write you check.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.020
No, no, you won't.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:17.840
I got enough of those to recap a time.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.240
Now, this time, you pay me in cash,

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.680
or I'll lock you out of your apartment.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:22.320
All right.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.540
You'll have your money today.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.270
I'm expecting an advance from MGM.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.300
MGM?

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:29.550
My grandmother.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.260
Get the money. You pay me first, right?

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:35.240
Right.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:38.540
If you tell me about that blonde who just walked out of here.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.150
Her name's Jane Hathaway.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.830
You've seen her on the roof, bird watching.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.280
Not her.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:45.980
Don't knock Miss Hathaway.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.200
She's a Vassar graduate, and she's really got it up here.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:55.660
Yeah, but I like it where the other girls got it.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:58.540
Forget about her.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:09:59.980
She wouldn't look twice at a bum like you.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.620
like you, a father's worth $95 million.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:05.740
95 million?

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:10.660
You want a lad who's living here with Ms. Hathaway

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:11.780
to learn how to be a secretary?

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:13.000
You're putting me on.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:13.900
True story.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:14.800
What's her name?

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:16.700
I told you to forget about her.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:18.900
One look at you and the family put a bounty on you.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.220
Why don't you get a haircut?

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.020
Cause this kind of hair is in now.

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:24.080
Besides, who's got three bucks?

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:28.670
Yeah, yeah, hold these.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:29.700
Now be careful.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.160
The first edition's on Audubon.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.450
These are paintings of birds.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:39.660
Well, what did you expect?

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:41.750
I thought Autobahn was a highway in Germany.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.940
Can I give you a piece of advice, Dick?

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:45.480
Bull.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.460
Paul Small, get acquainted with Miss Hathaway.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.540
Maybe you can learn something.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:51.200
It's a good idea, Mr. Finney.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.180
There is something I could learn from her.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.040
Well, you finally started to listen.

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.700
Look at the books this girl's got in this apartment.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:10:59.960
History, music.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:00.560
All right.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:01.520
Poetry.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:02.140
Birds.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:03.300
Right.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.620
Miss Hathaway is a true intellectual.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.950
You've given me some good advice, Mr. Finney, and I really appreciate it.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:13.950
Well, remember the overdue rent when the loot comes in from YGM.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:16.540
YGM.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:18.640
Your grandmother.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:21.730
Thank you.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:41.020
Mr. Finney, checking to see if you brought home any more animals.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.570
I'm terribly sorry for the intrusion, but this is an emergency.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.820
emergency yes I saw a summer tanager fly over the top of the building a summer

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:55.920
tanager yes it's quite a rare bird and I'm certain I spotted one I was right

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:56.860
there he is

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:00.480
Oh, my goodness.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:04.240
Oh, hold still, you elusive little beauty,

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.840
so I can focus on a close-up.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:08.180
Oh, this would be priceless.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:14.060
Yes, sir.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:15.040
What?

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:16.160
He flew away.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:18.080
Tragedy.

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:19.790
A summer tanager this time of year,

00:12:19.810 --> 00:12:22.130
it's almost unheard of.

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.860
Oh, are you interested in birds?

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:25.820
Oh, intensely.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.700
I'm a birdwatcher.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:29.980
Well, I had no idea there were...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:37.240
of us in the building oh i i've seen you briefly in passing i'm i'm jade hathaway forgive me in all

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:45.440
the excitement i neglected to introduce myself i'm robert audubon not audubon of the audubon

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:53.170
society well i'm a descendant of john james audubon oh marvelous what what an honor this is

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:53.770
Please.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.980
I don't like to capitalize on the family name.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:04.960
I can't tell you what a thrill this is.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.600
Oh, forgive me.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.860
This is my roommate, Ellie Mae Clappett,

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.860
Mr. Robert Audubon.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:12.210
Howdy.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:12.590
Hi.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.980
Well, I hope you're enjoying the show.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.360
our paths will cross again.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.690
As do I, Mr. Audubon.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:19.620
Huh? Bob.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:21.880
Jane.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:26.960
Oh, by the way,

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:28.290
forgive my appearance

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:29.550
for the last couple of months.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.260
been in the wilds of Canada.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.120
Well, I haven't had a chance to get to the barber.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:36.380
Will you by any chance in Canada to...

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.450
Photograph the almost extinct...

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.710
Ross's snow goose.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.870
Say you are an ornithologist.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:44.720
Coming from you, that is.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:46.100
I praise indeed.

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:48.730
Till we meet again.

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:50.070
Au revoir.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.640
Oh, uh, nice meeting you, Miss, uh...

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:55.680
I might clamp it.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:56.370
Thank you.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.080
Goodbye.

